# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: I-map ang mga classical input sa isang quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay maps every numerical input feature onto one qubit, so the first step is to turn the raw table into numerical features.\n"
msgstr "Minamapa ng Rimay ang bawat numerical input feature sa isang qubit, kaya ang unang hakbang ay gawing numerical na mga feature ang raw na table.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the dataset {#load-the-dataset}"
msgstr "I-load ang dataset {#load-the-dataset}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the German credit dataset directly from OpenML. The `class` column holds the label: `good` for applicants who repaid their credit and `bad` for those who did not.\n"
msgstr "I-load ang German credit dataset direkta mula sa OpenML. Ang column na `class` ang may hawak ng label: `good` para sa mga aplikanteng nakabayad ng kredito at `bad` para sa mga hindi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encode the features {#encode-the-features}"
msgstr "I-encode ang mga feature {#encode-the-features}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convert the label to a binary value, and one-hot encode the 13 categorical columns. The code drops the first category of each column to avoid redundant features, which results in 48 numerical features.\n"
msgstr "I-convert ang label sa binary na halaga, at i-one-hot encode ang 13 categorical na column. Tinatanggal ng code ang unang category ng bawat column para iwasan ang redundant na mga feature, kaya 48 numerical na feature ang lalabas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Split into training and test sets {#split-into-training-and-test-sets}"
msgstr "Hatiin sa training at test set {#split-into-training-and-test-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hold back 20% of the applicants as a test set. A stratified split keeps the share of good and bad credits equal in both sets.\n"
msgstr "Itabi ang 20% ng mga aplikante bilang test set. Pinapanatili ng stratified split na pantay ang proporsyon ng good at bad na kredito sa dalawang set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Establish a classical baseline {#establish-a-classical-baseline}"
msgstr "Gumawa ng classical baseline {#establish-a-classical-baseline}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Train a random forest on the classical features. In Step 4, you compare the quantum-transformed features against its metrics.\n"
msgstr "Mag-train ng random forest sa mga classical na feature. Sa Step 4, ikukumpara mo ang mga quantum-transformed na feature sa mga metric nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the data to Rimay {#upload-the-data-to-rimay}"
msgstr "I-upload ang data sa Rimay {#upload-the-data-to-rimay}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay reads its inputs from CSV files that you upload to the function. The features and the labels go into separate files. You also upload the test set, so that Rimay maps it with the same mapping it fits on the training set.\n"
msgstr "Binabasa ng Rimay ang mga input nito mula sa mga CSV file na ina-upload mo sa function. Magkahiwalay na file ang mga feature at ang mga label. Ina-upload mo rin ang test set, para imapa ito ng Rimay gamit ang parehong mapping na na-fit sa training set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize the problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pag-execute sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay builds and transpiles the circuits for the processor you select, so there is no circuit to optimize by hand. Specify the number of shots per circuit, within the following constraints:\n"
msgstr "Binubuo at tina-transpile ng Rimay ang mga circuit para sa processor na pipiliin mo, kaya walang circuit na kailangang i-optimize nang mano-mano. Tukuyin ang bilang ng shot kada circuit, sa loob ng mga sumusunod na limitasyon:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every feature needs one qubit, so the processor must have at least as many qubits as the dataset has features.\n"
msgstr "Kailangan ng bawat feature ng isang qubit, kaya dapat kasing dami man lang ng mga feature ng dataset ang qubit ng processor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay runs one circuit per row, training and test rows together. A single job can request at most 10 million executions, so the number of rows times `shots` must stay within that budget.\n"
msgstr "Nagpapatakbo ang Rimay ng isang circuit kada row, training at test row nang magkasama. Isang job ay puwedeng humiling ng hanggang 10 milyong execution lang, kaya dapat manatili sa budget na iyon ang bilang ng row na i-multiply sa `shots`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check both limits before you submit the job.\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang dalawang limitasyon bago mo i-submit ang job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"A job must also finish within 24 hours, including the time its circuits wait in the queue, or it is stopped without a result.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Dapat ding matapos ang isang job sa loob ng 24 oras, kasama ang oras na naghihintay ang mga circuit nito sa pila, kung hindi ay ihihinto ito nang walang resulta.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the function size {#calculate-the-function-size}"
msgstr "Kuwentahin ang function size {#calculate-the-function-size}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every job runs at a function size, `S`, `M`, or `L`, which selects the compute resources it runs on. For Rimay, the size depends on the number of rows that a job maps, training and test rows together. If you request a size that is too small, the job fails with error `4600`. For the sizes and their limits, see [Function sizes](/guides/kipu-rimay#function-sizes) in the Rimay guide.\n"
msgstr "Tumatakbo ang bawat job sa isang function size, `S`, `M`, o `L`, na pumipili ng compute resources na gagamitin nito. Para sa Rimay, nakadepende ang size sa bilang ng row na minamapa ng isang job, training at test row nang magkasama. Kung humiling ka ng size na masyadong maliit, magfa-fail ang job na may error na `4600`. Para sa mga size at limitasyon nila, tingnan ang [Function sizes](/guides/kipu-rimay#function-sizes) sa Rimay guide.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following cell defines the size calculator. It runs on your machine, reads only the data that you pass to it, and submits nothing.\n"
msgstr "Dinedefine ng sumusunod na cell ang size calculator. Tumatakbo ito sa makina mo, binabasa lang ang data na ipinasa mo rito, at walang sinusubmit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass the data sets in the same order as the files in `input_file`, together with the mode of the run:\n"
msgstr "Ipasa ang mga data set sa parehong ayos ng mga file sa `input_file`, kasama ang mode ng run:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Step 3: I-execute gamit ang Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run Rimay in `fit-transform` mode. It fits a quantum feature mapping on `x_train.csv` and `y_train.csv`, and maps both the training and the test sets with it. The order of the files in `input_file` matters. List the training features, the training labels, and then the optional test features. Pass the size that you calculated as `function_size`.\n"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang Rimay sa `fit-transform` mode. Magfi-fit ito ng quantum feature mapping sa `x_train.csv` at `y_train.csv`, at imamapa nito ang training at test set gamit iyon. Mahalaga ang ayos ng mga file sa `input_file`. Ilista ang training features, ang training labels, at pagkatapos ang opsyonal na test features. Ipasa ang size na kinuwenta mo bilang `function_size`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Monitor the job {#monitor-the-job}"
msgstr "I-monitor ang job {#monitor-the-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the status of the job while it runs. `job.result()` blocks until the job has finished.\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang status ng job habang tumatakbo ito. Hihinto ang `job.result()` hanggang matapos ang job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result holds a `mapping_id`, which identifies the mapping that this run fitted. You do not need it in this tutorial, because the test set was mapped in the same run. Record this ID if you want to map new rows later with `mode=\"transform\"`. It is the only way to access the fitted mapping, and without it, you must fit and pay for a new one. The mapping is built for the qubit layout of this processor, so a later `transform` run must pass the same `backend_name`.\n"
msgstr "May `mapping_id` ang result, na tumutukoy sa mapping na na-fit ng run na ito. Hindi mo ito kailangan sa tutorial na ito, dahil namapa ang test set sa parehong run. I-record ang ID na ito kung gusto mong magmapa ng mga bagong row sa susunod gamit ang `mode=\"transform\"`. Ito lang ang paraan para ma-access ang na-fit na mapping, at kung wala ito, kailangan mong mag-fit at magbayad ng bago. Binuo ang mapping para sa qubit layout ng processor na ito, kaya dapat ipasa ng susunod na `transform` run ang parehong `backend_name`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return the result in the desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-the-result-in-the-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Step 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang result sa nais na classical na format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-the-result-in-the-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download the quantum-transformed features {#download-the-quantum-transformed-features}"
msgstr "I-download ang mga quantum-transformed na feature {#download-the-quantum-transformed-features}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download the files that the job wrote, by using the names in `output_files`. Each name starts with the job ID, so the files of this run stay available after later runs. Pass `target_name` so that each file is saved under its own name.\n"
msgstr "I-download ang mga file na isinulat ng job, gamit ang mga pangalan sa `output_files`. Nagsisimula ang bawat pangalan sa job ID, kaya mananatiling available ang mga file ng run na ito pagkatapos ng mga susunod na run. Ipasa ang `target_name` para mase-save ang bawat file sa sarili nitong pangalan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Train on the quantum-transformed features {#train-on-the-quantum-transformed-features}"
msgstr "Mag-train sa mga quantum-transformed na feature {#train-on-the-quantum-transformed-features}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Train a random forest on the quantum-transformed features alone.\n"
